# SignPath approval follow-up

When the user says SignPath is **approved**, **accepted**, **live**, or that they have SignPath **org/API credentials**, do **not** stop at congratulations. Immediately drive this checklist (implement what you can; list what only they can do):

## Checklist (in order)

1. **Confirm secrets/vars in GitHub** (they paste values; never commit secrets):
   - Secret: SIGNPATH_API_TOKEN
   - Variables: SIGNPATH_ORGANIZATION_ID, SIGNPATH_PROJECT_SLUG, SIGNPATH_SIGNING_POLICY_SLUG
2. **SignPath project UI** (guide them if needed):
   - GitHub repo linked as trusted build system
   - Artifact configuration slug dumper-apps-exe matches .signpath/artifact-configurations/dumper-apps-exe.xml
   - Signing policy exists (approver = Sinedrone-Sentinel)
3. **Cut / verify a dumper release** that runs Build Executables on Release with SignPath enabled (signed DumperApps.exe on the GitHub Release)
4. **Flip the UI flag**: set SIGNPATH_SIGNING_LIVE = true in src/config/trustBadges.ts, open a PR assigned to @Sinedrone-Sentinel, wait for green CI
5. Propose a Site Update only if they want ticker news; wait for numbered approval

Canonical human-readable copy of this list: docs/TRUST_AND_SIGNING.md section **SignPath — YOUR next steps after approval**.

Do **not** set SIGNPATH_SIGNING_LIVE = true before a signed release is confirmed.
